# SDK Definition: No Default Type Parameters

`units/shared/@sdk.d.ts` must never use default type arguments (e.g. `T = unknown`, `T = void`). Every generic must be explicit so callers are forced to declare intent.

## Rule

Never write:
```ts
function queueWorker<TData, TResult = unknown>(...)
function workflow<TInput, TOutput = void>(...)
```

Always write:
```ts
function queueWorker<TData, TResult>(...)
function workflow<TInput, TOutput>(...)
```

## Callers must be explicit

When a worker or workflow has no meaningful return, the correct type is `never` (always throws) or `void` (returns nothing):

```ts
// ❌
export default queueWorker<Input>({ ... })

// ✅ — process always throws
export type Output = never;
export default queueWorker<Input, never>({ ... })

// ✅ — process returns nothing
export type Output = void;
export default queueWorker<Input, void>({ ... })

// ✅ — process returns a value
export type Output = { processed: true };
export default queueWorker<Input, Output>({ ... })
```

Same rule applies to `workflow<TInput, TOutput>` and any future SDK generics.
